.\" sliver-config(5). A test checks that every module type, common module key, context key and
.\" bar gesture known to crates/sliver-config is listed here.
.TH SLIVER\-CONFIG 5 2026-11-06 "sliver 0.1.0" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sliver\-config \- Touch Bar configuration (config.toml)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sliver/config.toml
.br
.I /etc/xdg/sliver/config.toml
.br
.I /usr/share/sliver/config.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Touch Bar is configured the way waybar is: everything on it is a
.IR module ,
every module is shaped by configuration
.RB ( format ,
states, gesture bindings), the look comes from a stylesheet
.RB ( sliver\-stylesheet (5)),
and zones, layers, layouts and rules are all defined by the user.
The invariants under
.B WHAT CANNOT BE CONFIGURED
are the only things a configuration can't change.
.PP
The file is TOML, and comments are allowed.
Keys are kebab\-case and use waybar's names wherever the concept maps, so waybar module blocks port with few changes
(or use
.BR "sliverctl config import\-waybar" ,
which converts waybar's JSONC module blocks).
.PP
The first file that exists in the order above is used, as in waybar.
The built\-in defaults are always merged underneath it, so the
.BR base ,
.B fn
and
.B media
layers, the
.BR default ,
.B fkeys
and
.B media
layouts and the control strip exist even with an empty file.
Any of them can be redefined.
tiny\-dfr's
.B MediaLayerDefault = true
is
.B [layers] base = \(dqmedia\(dq
with
.BR "fn = \(dqfkeys\(dq" .
.PP
.BR sliver\-agent (1)
watches the file, its includes and the stylesheet (and the directories they live in, so
rename\-saves and a file created later both count), and applies changes when they are saved.
.B sliverctl reload
and
.B SIGUSR2
to
.B sliver\-agent
reload at once.
An invalid configuration is never applied: the last good one stays live, and the errors are listed by
.BR "sliverctl status" .
Unknown keys produce warnings, not errors.
Check a file with
.BR "sliverctl config check" .
.PP
.BR sliver\-settings (1)
edits the same files and keeps their comments and formatting.
Arrays replace rather than merge, so when it edits a zone or a group that comes from the built\-ins or
an include, it first copies that layout's whole zone list (or the group's member list) into your file.
When the configuration in use is a system file, the new user file
.BR include s
it.
.SS Profiles
A profile is a whole configuration to switch to, such as \(lqWork\(rq or \(lqPresenting\(rq.
.B default
is the file above; any other profile is
.BI ~/.config/sliver/profiles/ name .toml
(names are letters, digits,
.B \-
and
.BR _ ).
A new profile starts as
.B include = [\(dq../config.toml\(dq]
(your main configuration plus its own changes);
.B sliverctl config profile new \-\-from
.I profile
copies another profile instead.
The active one is named in
.BR ~/.config/sliver/active\-profile ,
so every way of switching works the same and survives restarts.
A name whose file is missing means
.BR default .
While a profile is active,
.B sliverctl config set
edits its file.
Switch with
.BI "sliverctl profile" " name" ,
.BI "sliverctl config profile use" " name"
(offline),
.BR Control1.SetProfile ,
or a
.B { profile = \fIname\fP }
action.
A profile that doesn't validate is refused, and the previous one stays live.
Rules switch layouts, never profiles.
.SH TOP\-LEVEL KEYS
.TP
.BR version " = 1"
Format version.
.TP
.BR include " = [" \fIpaths\fP ]
Other files to merge in.
Paths are relative to the including file, and
.B ~
and globs work.
Tables are merged deeply, the including file wins, and earlier includes win over later ones.
Arrays are replaced, not concatenated.
Includes may nest up to 8 levels; a cycle is an error.
Relative paths in an included file
.RB ( icon ,
.BR stylesheet ,
an
.B image
module's
.BR path )
are relative to that file, so a shared theme directory can carry its own icons.
.TP
.BR stylesheet " = " \fIpath\fP
Default:
.B style.css
next to the configuration.
.B style\-dark.css
and
.B style\-light.css
follow the desktop's color scheme when present.
.TP
.BR theme " = " sliver | light | high\-contrast | classic
The built\-in theme under the stylesheet (default
.BR sliver ).
See
.BR sliver\-stylesheet (5).
.SH [bar]
.TP
.B name
Becomes a CSS class on the bar.
.TP
.BR spacing ", " margin
Pixels between modules, and around the strip.
.TP
.BR fn\-mode " = " hold | toggle
What the Fn key does with the
.B fn
layer.
.TP
.BR fire\-on " = " press | release
When taps fire, by default.
Each module can override it.
.SH [display]
.TP
.BR brightness " = " adaptive | fixed
Adaptive follows the main screen.
.TP
.BR max\-brightness " = " 0\-255
Scaled to the bar's own range: bars with a three\-step backlight (off, dim, full) never turn off
from a low setting.
.TP
.BR dim\-after ", " off\-after
Durations (default 30s and 60s), or
.BR \(dqnever\(dq .
\(lqOff\(rq is backlight 0.
The first touch on a dark bar only wakes it and fires nothing.
The bar is also off while the lid is closed.
.TP
.BR pixel\-shift " = " true | false
Moves the whole picture by up to 11 pixels along the bar and 2 across it, one pixel every 15
seconds, to spread OLED wear.
Touches are mapped back, and nothing moves while the bar is dark.
Keep content 11 pixels in from both ends while it's on.
.TP
.BR curve " = " [[ \fIscreen\fP ", " \fIbar\fP "], ...]"
How adaptive brightness maps the main screen's brightness to the bar's.
Both are percentages from 0 to 100 (of the screen's maximum, and of
.BR max\-brightness ),
with 2 to 16 points and the screen values strictly increasing.
Between points the bar follows a straight line, and beyond the first and last point it stays flat.
Left out, the bar follows tiny\-dfr's square\-root curve.
For example, a bar that stays readable on a dark screen:
.BR "curve = [[0, 20], [50, 60], [100, 100]]" .
.TP
.B [display.on\-battery]
.BR max\-brightness ,
.B dim\-after
and
.B off\-after
to use instead while running on battery (from UPower).
Keys left out keep their
.B [display]
values.
For example, a dimmer bar that turns off sooner:
.B max\-brightness = 60
and
.BR "off\-after = \(dq20s\(dq" .
.SH [apps], [providers] AND [api]
What apps and scripts that use the D\-Bus API may put on the bar.
Your own layouts and rules always win over them.
.TP
.BR [apps."\fIapp\-id\fP"]
.B controls
(default true): the app's items (or a provider's) may fill
.BR app\-controls .
.B whole\-bar
(default true): a modal context of the app may cover the bar beyond its first zone.
.B pin
= \fIprovider\fP: only that provider fills the app's controls.
App ids match case\-insensitively, with a
.B .desktop
suffix ignored.
.B [apps."*"]
sets the defaults for every app.
.TP
.BR [providers."\fIid\fP"]
The D\-Bus provider id (a Flatpak or Snap id when sandboxed).
.B show
(default true): false hides it everywhere, in Status items and App controls.
.B allow
(default false): let a sandboxed provider show status items.
.B order
= \fIn\fP: its place among status items (lower first; unlisted ones follow, by id).
.TP
.B [api]
.B target
(default true): let clients put controls on the bar for another app.
.PP
The agent applies changes to these tables on reload, without restarting clients.
.SH LAYERS, LAYOUTS AND RULES
.TP
.B [layers]
Maps each layer name to its default layout.
.B base
and
.B fn
are reserved (Fn shows
.BR fn ,
as
.B fn\-mode
says).
Any other name is a custom layer, opened by a
.B layer
action.
.TP
.BI [layer\-options. name ]
.B timeout
(a duration) and
.B close\-button
(a boolean).
.TP
.BI [layouts. name ]
.B extends
names a parent layout.
.B zones
is an ordered array of tables with
.BR name ,
.B modules
(module ids or inline tables),
.B width
.RB ( \(dqauto\(dq ,
pixels or
.BR \(dqfill\(dq ),
.B align
.RB ( start ,
.BR center ,
.BR end ;
like waybar's
.BR fixed\-center ),
.B module\-width
(the default width for the zone's modules, for example
.B \(dqfill\(dq
for tiny\-dfr\-style equal keys) and
.BR class .
Any number of zones with any names is allowed; the shipped
.BR esc ,
.B main
and
.B controls
are a convention.
A child layout's zone replaces the parent's zone of the same name, in place (the whole zone, not
merged).
New zone names go at the end, unless
.B zone\-order
lists the order.
Zones become stylesheet classes
.RB ( .zone\- \fIname\fP ).
.TP
.B [[rules]]
.BR name ,
.B when
(a condition),
.B layer
(default
.BR base )
and
.BR layout .
Rules are checked top to bottom, and the first match wins.
If none matches, the
.B [layers]
default applies.
.PP
The built\-in base layout's main zone is
.B app\-controls
followed by
.B group/fkeys
(F1\(enF12, shown while no app fills App controls), so the bar shows F\-keys until the focused app
publishes controls.
The control strip is the drawer group
.BR group/control\-strip ;
nothing about it is hard\-coded.
.PP
The built\-in rules are one lock\-screen rule,
.B when = { locked = true }
showing layout
.B locked
(media keys, brightness and volume sliders, mute, and Esc where there's no physical Escape key).
Like any array, your own
.B rules
replace it, and
.B rules = []
removes it.
Whatever the rules say, published app items,
.B custom/
output, notifications, window titles and the taskbar are never shown while the screen is locked.
.SH CONDITIONS
A condition
.RB ( when ,
on rules and on modules) is a table of context keys, all of which must match.
.B any = [{...}, {...}]
needs one of the sub\-tables to match, and
.B not = {...}
negates.
A value can be a literal (bool, number or string), an array (one of),
.BR "{ regex = \(dq...\(dq }" ,
.BR "{ contains = \(dq...\(dq }" ,
.BR "{ below = N }" ,
.B "{ above = N }"
or
.BR "{ between = [A, B] }" .
Keys are case\-insensitive, and
.B \-
and
.B _
are interchangeable.
An unknown or unavailable key never matches.
.PP
Context keys:
.TP
Focus
.BR app_id ,
.BR desktop_id ,
.BR title ,
.BR pid ,
.BR fullscreen ,
.BR floating ,
.BR xwayland .
.B app_id
compares case\-insensitively and also matches the app's
.B .desktop
id (through
.BR StartupWMClass ),
so
.B firefox
and
.B org.mozilla.firefox
both work.
.TP
Desktop
.BR workspace ,
.BR workspace_name ,
.BR special_workspace ,
.BR monitor ,
.B monitors
(a count),
.BR external_display ,
.BR keyboard_layout ,
.B submap
(Hyprland submap, sway mode),
.B screencast
.TP
Session
.BR locked ,
.BR idle ,
.BR sleeping ,
.BR dnd ,
.BR dark_mode ,
.B caffeine
.TP
Power
.BR on_battery ,
.BR battery_pct ,
.BR battery_state ,
.BR lid_closed ,
.B power_profile
.TP
Media and audio
.B media_status
.RB ( playing ,
.BR paused ,
.BR stopped ,
.BR none ),
.BR media_player ,
.BR media_title ,
.BR media_artist ,
.BR mic_muted ,
.BR output_muted ,
.B volume
.TP
Other
.B brightness
(the main screen, percent),
.B time
.RB ( HH:MM ),
.B weekday
.RB ( mon ,
\&...),
.BR physical_esc ,
.BR layer ,
.BR layout ,
.B app_controls
(true while an app fills App controls, so a layout can show something else when none does)
.PP
.B layout
is the layout the rules chose, so only module conditions can use it; a rule on it never matches.
User variables set with
.B sliverctl var set
can be used too.
.PP
Which window has focus comes from the compositor: Hyprland, sway, niri and other wlroots
compositors are read directly; GNOME and KDE need the extension or KWin script that ship with
sliver.
.B locked
believes, in order, the desktop's screensaver
.B ActiveChanged
signal, logind's
.B LockedHint
on GNOME and KDE, and elsewhere whether a known locker
.RB ( hyprlock ,
.BR swaylock ,
.BR gtklock ,
.BR waylock ,
.BR i3lock ,
.BR physlock )
is running.
.SH MODULES
A module reference is
.IR type ,
.IR type # instance
or
.IR namespace / name [# instance ],
as in waybar, and is configured in
.BI [modules." reference "]\fR.
.B battery#bat2
is a second battery; the instance becomes a CSS class
.RB ( #battery.bat2 ).
.B key/\fIName\fP
(for example
.BR key/F1 ,
.BR key/PlayPause )
needs no block: it is a key with a label and icon and
.BR "on\-tap = { key = \(dq\fIName\fP\(dq }" ;
a block, if present, is merged on top.
A zone's
.B modules
list can also contain inline tables with a
.B type
key (a reference without an instance, such as
.B \(dqkey/F1\(dq
or
.BR \(dqcustom\(dq ),
for example
.BR "{ type = \(dqcustom\(dq, format = \(dqTTY1\(dq, on\-tap = { keys = [\(dqLeftCtrl\(dq, \(dqLeftAlt\(dq, \(dqF1\(dq] } }" .
An empty
.B icon = \(dq\(dq
or
.B format = \(dq\(dq
clears a default.
Built\-in modules have no powers that user modules lack: they produce the same output fields as
.BR custom/ ,
take the same common keys, and are styled, bound and placed the same way.
.SS Common keys
Every module accepts these.
waybar's names are accepted as aliases:
.B on\-click
.RB ( on\-tap ),
.B on\-double\-click
.RB ( on\-double\-tap ),
.B on\-click\-right
.RB ( on\-hold ),
.B on\-click\-release
.RB ( on\-release ),
.B on\-scroll\-up
.RB ( on\-swipe\-right ),
.B on\-scroll\-down
.RB ( on\-swipe\-left ),
.B smooth\-scrolling\-threshold
.RB ( swipe\-threshold ).
.TP
.B format
Text with
.BI { placeholder }
and
.BI { name : spec }\fR.
The placeholders depend on the module (see
.BR "Module types" ).
.TP
.BR format\-alt ", " format\- \fIstate\fP ", " format\- \fIstatus\fP ", " format\- \fIstatus\fP \- \fIstate\fP
Alternatives (for example
.BR format\-charging ,
.BR format\-critical ).
A tap toggles
.B format\-alt
when
.B on\-tap
is unset, and so does the
.B { format = \(dqtoggle\-alt\(dq }
action.
.TP
.B format\-icons
An array (indexed by percentage, low to high), a table (by alt, status, state, then
.BR default ;
entries may be arrays), or a string.
An entry is text (a glyph) or
.B { icon = \(dqname\-or\-path\(dq }
for an image.
.TP
.B states
Name to threshold on the percentage, for example
.BR "{ warning = 30, critical = 15 }" .
Adds a class and selects
.BR format\- \fIstate\fP .
.TP
.B icon
XDG icon name, file path, or
.BI tiny\-dfr: name
(tiny\-dfr's icon directories).
Paths can be absolute,
.BR ~/... ,
or relative to the configuration's directory; a name ending in
.BR .png ,
.B .svg
or
.B .svgz
is a file.
.TP
.BR icon\-theme ", " icon\-size
The icon theme for this module, and the icon size in pixels.
.TP
.B width
.BR \(dqauto\(dq ,
pixels,
.B \(dqfill\(dq
or
.BR "{ fill = N }" .
.B expand = true
means
.BR \(dqfill\(dq .
.TP
.BR min\-length ", " max\-length ", " align ", " justify
Label length in characters (ellipsized past
.BR max\-length ),
and alignment within the module.
.TP
.B class
Extra CSS classes (a string or an array).
.TP
.B when
A condition.
The module is shown only while it holds, for example the battery only on battery.
.TP
.B hide\-empty\-text
Hide the module when its text is empty.
.TP
.B fire\-on
.B press
or
.BR release ,
overriding
.BR "[bar] fire\-on" .
.B key/
modules default to press.
.TP
.B repeat
Hold\-to\-repeat, the default for
.BR key/ .
.TP
.B swipe\-threshold
Swipe distance in pixels (default 40).
.TP
.BR on\-tap ", " on\-double\-tap ", " on\-hold ", " on\-release ", " on\-swipe\-left ", " on\-swipe\-right ", " on\-drag ", " on\-update
Actions (see ACTIONS).
A hold is 500\ ms.
Only gestures a module binds are recognized, so its taps fire at once unless
.B on\-double\-tap
is bound, which delays them.
.B on\-drag
runs at most every 50\ ms, always with the final value; a slider reports 0\(en100 along its track,
other modules the position on the bar.
.TP
.B actions
Gesture to built\-in module action, for example
.B { on\-hold = \(dqtoggle\-mute\(dq }
on audio.
Built\-in behaviour (a slider's drag, audio's tap to mute, mpris's tap and swipes) goes through these
same actions, and your own
.B on\-*
bindings win over it.
.TP
.BR menu ", " menu\-trigger
An array of
.B {label, icon, on\-tap}
shown as a temporary sub\-bar, and the gesture that opens it (default tap, or hold when the module
also has a tap action).
The sub\-bar puts a close button where the module was (a second tap there, or on empty space,
dismisses it), then the entries, each as wide as its label.
It covers the layout except its first zone, and its last when there are more than two, and closes
after 5\ s untouched.
Labels can use the module's own placeholders, and a
.B { module\-action = \fIname\fP }
entry acts on the module that opened it, so on
.B taskbar
.B menu = [{ label = \(dqClose {name}\(dq, on\-tap = { module\-action = \(dqclose\(dq } }]
asks before closing a window.
Picking an entry runs it and closes the sub\-bar.
.I examples/config/power\-menu.toml
is a power menu to copy or include.
.TP
.B interval
Polling period
.RB ( \(dq5s\(dq )
or
.BR \(dqonce\(dq .
The floor is 100\ ms, and anything under 1\ s gets a warning.
.TP
.B pass\-through
For
.B app/
modules: also send the gesture to the app when a user
.B on\-*
binding exists.
By default the user's binding replaces the app's event.
.TP
.B slider
.B true
draws the module as a press\-and\-slide slider over its value (backlight, keyboard backlight and
audio levels, or a custom module's
.BR value ).
.IB type /slider
is the same as
.I type
with
.BR "slider = true" .
Dragging sets the value, and
.B on\-drag
gets it as
.BR {value} .
.B collapsed = true
shows just the icon until touched: it opens on press, sliding without lifting moves the value from
where it was, and it closes 5\ s after the last touch.
.SS Format strings
The format used is the first that exists of
.B format\-alt
(when toggled),
.BI format\- status \- state\fR,
.BI format\- status\fR,
.BI format\- state\fR,
.BR format ,
then the module's default.
.B states
count lower as worse for battery\-like modules
.RB ( "warning = 30"
means 30% or less) and higher as worse for cpu, memory and temperature.
An array
.B format\-icons
of
.I n
entries is indexed by
.IR "floor(percentage / (100 / n))" .
An
.B {icon}
that is an image renders as empty text and the image is drawn as the module's icon.
A
.I spec
is the module's own (strftime for the clock), else
.BR [[\fIfill\fP]\fIalign\fP][0][\fIwidth\fP][.\fIprecision\fP] .
Unknown placeholders render literally, and a bad format string is a validation error.
.PP
Format output is markup, a subset of Pango's: tags
.BR b ,
.BR i ,
.BR u ,
.BR s ,
.BR big ,
.BR small ,
.BR sub ,
.BR sup ,
.B tt
and
.BR span ,
whose attributes are
.B foreground
.RB ( fgcolor ,
.BR color ),
.BR weight ,
.BR style ,
.B size
(keywords,
.IR NN% ,
.BR larger ,
.BR smaller ),
.BR underline ,
.B strikethrough
and
.B font_family
.RB ( face );
entities
.BR &amp; ,
.BR &lt; ,
.BR &gt; ,
.BR &quot; ,
.B &apos;
and
.BR &# \fIN\fP; .
Background colours, baseline shift and font descriptions are ignored (stylesheets cover them).
Bad markup keeps its text and reports a warning; it never blanks a module.
.SS Module types
Each type's placeholders, keys and gestures, beyond the common keys.
waybar's names
.RB ( pulseaudio ,
.BR hyprland/workspaces ,
.BR idle_inhibitor ,
\&...) are accepted as aliases.
.TP
.BI key/ name
Esc, F1\(enF24, media keys and other keys, sent by
.BR sliverd (8)
through uinput.
Key names are tiny\-dfr's (see ACTIONS).
A module whose only binding is a key tap is handled by
.B sliverd
itself: it presses the instant a finger lands, and keeps working if the agent hangs.
.TP
.B spacer
Empty;
.B width
sets its size.
.TP
.B clock
.BI {: strftime }
and
.BR {timezone} .
.B locale
(\fBde_DE\fP, or \fBde_DE.UTF\-8\fP) names days and months in that language.
.B timezone
(\fBAsia/Tokyo\fP), or
.B timezones
(a list;
.B \(dq\(dq
is local time) to cycle through by swiping.
Unknown names show a warning sign on the module.
.TP
.B battery
.BR {capacity} ,
.BR {time} ,
.BR {status} ;
status formats such as
.BR format\-charging .
.TP
.BR backlight ", " kbd\-backlight
The screen and keyboard backlight:
.BR {percent} .
.B backlight/slider
and
.B kbd\-backlight/slider
are the slider forms.
.TP
.B audio
The default output:
.BR {volume} ,
the
.B muted
status; tap mutes.
.B node = \(dqsource\(dq
(say,
.BR audio#mic )
is the microphone
.RB ( \(dqsink\(dq ,
the default, is the output).
.B audio/slider
is the slider form.
.TP
.B mpris
.BR {title} ,
.BR {artist} ,
.BR {album} ,
.BR {player} ,
.BR {status_icon} ,
.B {position}
and
.B {length}
.RI ( m:ss ;
a format that shows
.B {position}
redraws each second while playing).
Tap plays or pauses, swipes skip, and hold switches to the next player when several run.
The album art is the icon (local files, or
.B http(s)
fetched once into
.IR ~/.cache/sliver/art ;
PNG and JPEG);
.B art = false
turns it off.
.B scrub = true
makes the module a progress slider that seeks on drag.
.TP
.B workspaces
One button per workspace of the focused output
.RB ( "all\-outputs = true"
for all), with classes
.BR .active ,
.BR .urgent ,
.BR .empty ,
.B .default
and
.B :checked
on the active one;
.BR {name} ,
.BR {id} ,
.BR {windows} .
Tap switches workspace.
.TP
.B window
.BR {title} ,
.BR {app_id} .
.B rewrite
as in waybar: a table of \fIregex\fP = \fIreplacement\fP, or an array of
.B { match, replace }
tables when order matters.
Every rule whose regex matches the whole title applies, in order
.RB ( $1
for captures).
.TP
.B mode
The compositor's submap or mode.
.TP
.B language
The keyboard layout.
Tap switches to the next one; hold opens a sub\-bar of the configured layouts (Hyprland, sway,
niri), unless the module has its own
.BR menu .
Placeholders
.BR {} ,
.B {short}
and
.BR {long} :
the layout name.
.TP
.B idle\-inhibitor
Caffeine: tap holds an idle inhibitor.
Status
.B activated
or
.BR deactivated .
.TP
.B dnd
Do Not Disturb, from the notification daemon; hidden when the daemon doesn't say.
Tap switches it on dunst, mako, swaync and KDE.
.TP
.B dark\-mode
The desktop's light or dark scheme (from the XDG portal); classes
.B .dark
and
.BR .light ,
.BR {state} .
Tap switches it on KDE and GNOME\-style desktops.
.TP
.BR screenshot ", " lock ", " power
.B screenshot
takes an interactive screenshot through the portal.
.B lock
locks the session through logind, so your locker runs.
.B power
opens a sub\-bar with Lock and Suspend on tap, and Reboot and Power off on hold, so those can't be
tapped by accident;
.B menu
replaces its entries.
.TP
.B power\-profiles
.BR {profile} .
.TP
.BR cpu ", " memory ", " temperature ", " disk ", " load
Read from
.I /proc
and
.I /sys
on
.B interval
(defaults: cpu, temperature and load 10\ s; memory and disk 30\ s), only while shown on a lit bar.
cpu:
.BR {usage} ,
.BR {load} ,
.BR {avg_frequency} ,
.B {spark}
(a text sparkline of the last 16 samples).
memory:
.BR {percentage} ,
.BR {used} ,
.BR {total} ,
.BR {avail} ,
.BR {swapPercentage} ,
.BR {swapUsed} ,
.BR {swapTotal} ,
.B {swapAvail}
(GiB).
load:
.BR {load1} ,
.BR {load5} ,
.BR {load15} .
temperature:
.BR {temperatureC} ,
.BR {temperatureF} ,
.BR {temperatureK} ;
keys
.BR thermal\-zone ,
.B hwmon\-path
and
.B critical\-threshold
(adds
.BR .critical );
the default source is the hottest sensor.
disk:
.BR {percentage_used} ,
.BR {percentage_free} ,
.BR {used} ,
.BR {free} ,
.B {total}
(GiB),
.BR {path} ;
key
.B path
(default
.BR / ).
.TP
.B network
From NetworkManager:
.BR {essid} ,
.BR {ifname} ,
.BR {signalStrength} ,
.BR {ipaddr} ,
.BR {state} ;
classes
.BR .wifi ,
.BR .ethernet ,
.BR .vpn ,
.BR .disconnected ,
.B .connecting
and
.B .off
(Wi\-Fi radio off); the percentage is the Wi\-Fi signal.
Tap switches the Wi\-Fi radio.
With an explicit
.B interval
only, throughput is read too:
.BR {bandwidthDownBytes} ,
.BR {bandwidthUpBytes} ,
.BR {bandwidthTotalBytes} ,
the same with
.BR Bits ,
and
.B {spark}
(download history).
Hidden without NetworkManager.
.TP
.B bluetooth
From BlueZ:
.BR {device_alias} ,
.BR {device_battery_percentage} ,
.BR {num_connections} ,
.BR {status} ;
classes
.BR .off ,
.BR .on ,
.BR .connected .
Tap switches the adapter.
Hidden without an adapter.
.TP
.B graph
.RB ( custom\-graph/ \fIname\fP )
A drawn sparkline of another module's percentage
.RB ( "source = \(dqcpu\(dq" ,
.BR \(dqmemory\(dq ,
.BR \(dqbattery\(dq ,
.BR \(dqcustom/x\(dq )
or of its own
.B exec
(printing a number, or JSON with
.BR percentage ),
sampled every
.B interval
(default 2\ s) while the bar is on.
.B samples
(default 30, newest at the right),
.B min
and
.B max
(default 0 and 100).
.B states
apply to the latest value.
Hidden until the first sample, and while locked.
.TP
.B systemd\-failed\-units
Failed units of the system and user managers:
.BR {nr_failed} ,
.BR {nr_failed_system} ,
.BR {nr_failed_user} ,
.BR {units} ;
.B format\-ok
(default \(lq\[OK]\(rq), classes
.B .degraded
and
.BR .ok .
Hidden while nothing failed unless
.BR "hide\-on\-ok = false" ;
.B system = false
or
.B user = false
leaves a manager out.
Tap lists the failed units; an entry shows its status in your terminal.
.TP
.B taskbar
One icon per window of the active workspace
.RB ( "all\-workspaces = true"
for all), from the app's
.B .desktop
entry.
Classes
.BR .focused ,
.B .urgent
and
.BI .app\- id
(lowercased, other characters as
.BR \- ).
.B {name}
(the app's name),
.BR {title} ,
.BR {app_id} ;
.B format\-focused
for the focused window's button.
Tap focuses, hold closes.
.B pinned = [\(dqorg.mozilla.firefox\(dq, \(dqkitty\(dq]
adds launchers first: a running pinned app is its window's button, an idle one starts the app on tap
(classes
.BR .pinned ,
.BR .running ,
.BR .idle ).
.TP
.B notifications
A bell with the latest notification's summary
.RB ( {summary} ,
.BR {app} ;
never the body) or the number open
.RB ( {count} );
classes
.BR .pending ,
.BR .none ,
.BR .dnd .
Tap invokes the default action (with
.BR makoctl ),
or dismisses; swipes dismiss.
.TP
.B emoji
As a button it opens the built\-in
.B emoji
layer
.RB ( "mode = \(dqbutton\(dq" ,
the default); with
.B mode = \(dqstrip\(dq
it is that layer: group tabs (recents first), one page of
.B columns
emoji (default 14), swipe to page.
Tapping types the emoji:
.B insert
is
.B auto
(wtype if installed, else the clipboard),
.BR wtype ,
.B paste
(replaces the clipboard) or
.BR copy .
Holding an emoji with skin tones offers them, and group pages then use the tone last picked.
The search tab spells a query on the bar with a letter row; every word of the query is a prefix of
the name.
Recents are kept in
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/sliver/emoji\-recents .
Classes
.B .emoji\-tone
and
.BR .emoji\-back .
.TP
.B timer
A countdown:
.B duration
(default 25m),
.BR {remaining} ,
.BR {minutes} ,
.BR {seconds} ;
the percentage is left for
.BR states .
Tap starts and pauses, hold resets, and it calls
.B notify\-send
at zero.
Status classes
.BR .idle ,
.BR .running ,
.BR .paused ,
.BR .finished .
.TP
.B image
A picture that fills the module's height at its aspect ratio:
.B path
(a file or an icon name), or
.B exec
printing a path, re\-run on
.B interval
or
.B signal
as for custom modules.
A changed file is picked up.
PNG, JPEG or SVG, kept at most 120 pixels tall.
Hidden without a picture, and while locked.
.TP
.B group
.RB ( group/ \fIname\fP )
See
.BR Groups .
.TP
.BR app\-controls ", " status\-items
Where items that apps publish go: App controls holds the focused app's, Status items holds
background status items, including StatusNotifierItems
.RB ( tray
is an alias).
A layout without them shows none.
Their
.B width
sizes the slot:
.B auto
fits the items; a pixel width reserves that much, even when empty, and drops the lowest\-priority
items that don't fit; while
.B fill
adds a share of the zone's leftover after the items.
.TP
.B app
.BI app/ provider # item
pins one published item anywhere, like any module, and
.BI app/ provider
a whole context.
Pinned items leave the placeholders.
.TP
.B custom
.RB ( custom/ \fIname\fP )
A user module (see
.BR "Custom modules" ).
With only
.B format
set, it is a static button.
.SS Groups
.BI group/ name
takes
.BR modules ,
.B orientation
.RB ( horizontal
or
.BR vertical ),
.B module\-width
(as on a zone) and
.BR drawer .
.B vertical
stacks children in two 30\-pixel rows, which suits display\-only modules; the check warns when a
stacked child has actions.
.PP
.B drawer
makes the first module the leader and hides the rest until the leader is tapped.
It is a table with
.B reveal
.RB ( tap ;
accepted for waybar's sake, a tap always opens it),
.B mode
.RB ( inline
expands in place and pushes neighbours;
.B bar
opens the rest as a sub\-bar with a close button),
.BR start\-expanded ,
.B collapse\-after
(closes again after that long without a touch),
.B children\-class
(replaces the
.B drawer\-child
class) and
.B transition\-left\-to\-right
.RB ( false
puts the leader after the rest, so it opens towards the left).
A drawer's modules appear at once; a stylesheet
.B transition: width
on the modules around it makes them glide.
.SS Custom modules
.BI custom/ name
runs scripts the way waybar does.
.TP
.BR exec ", " exec\-if
The command and its guard (run only if the guard exits 0).
Commands run with
.BR "sh \-c" ,
as you and never as root, in their own process group (a timeout kills the whole tree), with
.BR no_new_privs ,
no stdin and at most 64\ KiB of output.
.TP
.BR interval ", " signal
Run on a timer, on
.B SIGRTMIN+\fIn\fP
to
.B sliver\-agent
or
.BR "sliverctl signal" .
With neither, the script runs continuously and each output line is an update.
Nothing runs while the bar is off or the screen is locked; everything re\-runs once when it comes back.
.TP
.B restart\-interval
For continuous scripts that exit (minimum 1\ s, doubling up to 60\ s while they keep dying quickly).
.TP
.B exec\-on\-event
Re\-run after an
.B on\-*
action (default true).
.TP
.B return\-type
.B \(dq\(dq
(lines: text, tooltip, class) or
.B \(dqjson\(dq
(one object per line with waybar's
.BR text ,
.BR alt ,
.B tooltip
(shown by a
.B {tooltip}
placeholder),
.B class
(a string or an array) and
.BR percentage ,
plus
.B icon
(a name or path),
.B value
(0\(en100, for
.BR "slider = true" )
and
.BR hidden ).
Built\-in modules produce exactly these fields, and so do published items and
.BR "sliverctl update" .
.TP
.BR escape ", " timeout ", " env
Escape markup in the output, per\-run timeout (default 2\ s), and extra environment.
Commands also get
.BR SLIVER_MODULE ,
.BR SLIVER_LAYER ,
.B SLIVER_LAYOUT
and
.BR SLIVER_APP_ID .
.PP
A failed or timed\-out run shows
.B !
with the
.B error
class, and the last line of stderr as its tooltip.
Updates are drawn only when the output changed, and at most 30 times a second.
.SH ACTIONS
An
.B on\-*
key takes one of:
.TP
.I \(dqcommand\(dq
A shell command.
.B {value}
is substituted for
.BR on\-drag .
.TP
.B { exec = [argv] }
No shell.
.IP
Commands start in their own process group, and under systemd in their own scope, so restarting
the agent doesn't kill apps opened from the bar.
.TP
.BR "{ key = \(dqF5\(dq }" ", " "{ keys = [\(dqLeftCtrl\(dq, \(dqLeftAlt\(dq, \(dqF1\(dq] }"
Key presses, honouring
.BR repeat .
A combo is pressed in order and released in reverse.
Key names are tiny\-dfr's
.RB ( F1 ,
.BR BrightnessDown ,
.BR PlayPause ,
\&...), matched case\-insensitively.
Letters, digits and punctuation mean the character on a US keyboard, and are sent as the key that
types that character in your keyboard layout, so
.B [\(dqLeftCtrl\(dq, \(dqZ\(dq]
is undo on AZERTY and QWERTZ too.
This needs a compositor that reports the layout (Hyprland); elsewhere, and for characters a layout
only has with Shift (AZERTY digits) or not at all (Greek), the US key position is sent.
.B SysRq
is refused.
.TP
.BR "{ layer = \(dqmedia\(dq, mode = \(dqtoggle\(dq }" ", " "{ close\-layer = true }"
.B mode
is
.B hold
(until that finger lifts),
.B toggle
or
.B oneshot
(closes after the next action taken in it).
.B close\-layer
returns to the layer underneath.
.TP
.B { layout = \fIname\fP }
Forces a layout until the context changes.
.TP
.B { profile = \fIname\fP }
Switches to another profile.
.TP
.BR "{ open = \(dqapp.desktop\(dq }" ", " "{ url = \fIU\fP }"
Launches an app by its desktop id, or opens a URL or file.
.TP
.B { dbus = { bus, dest, path, interface, method, args } }
.B bus
is
.B session
(default) or
.BR system .
.B args
are converted to the method's real types, read from its introspection
.RB ( [false]
is a
.BR b ,
.B [7]
a
.B u
if the method wants one; a table is
.BR a{sv} );
on a mismatch nothing is sent and the error is logged.
.TP
.BR "{ signal = N }" ", " "{ update = \(dqcustom/vpn\(dq }"
Refresh modules.
.TP
.B { format = \(dqtoggle\-alt\(dq }
Toggles
.BR format\-alt .
.TP
.B { module\-action = \fIname\fP }
A built\-in action of the module, such as
.B next\-player
on
.BR mpris .
.TP
.I [ step, ... ]
A macro.
Steps can include
.BR "{ sleep = \(dq100ms\(dq }" .
Macros are capped at 32 steps and 10\ s.
.PP
Durations are written
.BR \(dq250ms\(dq ,
.BR \(dq5s\(dq ,
.B \(dq2m\(dq
or as a bare number of seconds.
.SH GESTURES
Bar\-wide gestures go in
.BR [gestures] ,
with the same action forms:
.TP
.BR two\-finger\-swipe\-left ", " two\-finger\-swipe\-right
Both fingers travel at least 60 pixels the same way.
Once a second finger lands, neither finger taps, holds, swipes or drags its module.
It fires once per contact.
Unbound, two fingers are just two touches.
.TP
.BR edge\-swipe\-from\-left ", " edge\-swipe\-from\-right
Starts within 48 pixels of that end of the bar and travels at least 80 pixels inward.
It takes precedence over that module's own swipe; a touch that doesn't move is still a tap, and
sliders keep their drag.
.PP
Gestures are recognized over every module except plain key buttons.
Those are pressed the instant a finger lands, so no bar gesture can start on one.
The bar reports no pressure and no hover, and is too short for vertical swipes.
.SH SCRIPTING FROM OUTSIDE
.BR sliverctl (1)
and the D\-Bus
.B Control1
interface reload the configuration, signal, update, tap, hold, show and hide modules, push, pop
and toggle layers, force a layout, show or hide the whole bar, get and set configuration keys
(written to the file, which then reloads), and render the bar, or how a file would look, to PNG.
.B SIGUSR1
to
.B sliver\-agent
toggles the bar, like waybar.
Hiding the bar leaves the safe hatch working.
.SH WHAT CANNOT BE CONFIGURED
Every layout, including the Fn layer, is fully editable and may drop Escape and the F\-keys.
Pressing Fn twice (within 400\ ms) and holding it always shows the built\-in F1\(enF12 layer (with
Esc first on bars that have no physical Escape key) for as long as Fn is held.
This is enforced by
.BR sliverd (8),
and no configuration, app or agent can change or block it.
The check only warns when the base and fn layers have no F1\(enF12,
or a bar without a physical Escape key has no Esc.
.PP
On bars without a physical Escape key (the 2170\-pixel models), the default configuration and the
tiny\-dfr importer put
.B key/Esc
first in the base and fn layers.
.PP
Touch targets are advice: the check warns when a module with an action is narrower than 80 pixels
(about 9\ mm), and more strongly below 60, but never refuses.
.PP
App items
.RB ( app\-controls ,
.BR status\-items ,
.BR app/ ),
.B custom/
output,
.BR image ,
.BR graph ,
notification text, media titles and art, window titles
.RB ( window ,
.BR taskbar )
and emoji recents are never shown on the lock screen.
By default notification text also stays off the bar while the screen is shared (the built\-in
.B when
of
.BR notifications ,
which you can remove).
.PP
Intervals have a 100\ ms floor, restarts a 1\ s floor, and scripts have timeouts.
Modal app contexts never cover your first zone.
A configuration error never reaches the bar: the last good configuration stays, and
.BR sliverd 's
built\-in layer is the backstop.
.SH WAYBAR FEATURES THAT DON'T APPLY
.TP
.BR layer ", " output ", " position ", " height ", " width ", " exclusive ", " passthrough ", " mode ", " ipc ", " id ", " modifier\-reset
There is one fixed panel, not a Wayland surface.
Use
.B [bar]
margin and spacing, and rules on
.BR monitor .
.TP
Several bars in one file
There is one physical bar: use layouts, rules and layers.
.TP
.BR start_hidden ", " on\-sigusr1
.B sliverctl bar hide
and
.BR toggle ,
and
.B SIGUSR1
toggles.
.TP
Hover, tooltips and mouse buttons
A touch strip has none:
.B tooltip
and
.B tooltip\-format
are warned about and ignored.
Use tap, double tap, hold, swipes and drag; a script's tooltip can be put in
.B format
as
.BR {tooltip} .
.TP
.B rotate
The bar is 60 pixels tall.
.TP
Drawer \fBtransition\-duration\fP
Animation belongs to the stylesheet:
.BR "transition: width" .
.TP
.B cffi
In\-process plugins could take the bar down: use
.B custom/
or the D\-Bus API.
.TP
GtkBuilder \fBmenu\-file\fP
Use
.BR menu .
.TP
Full Pango markup
Only the subset under
.B Format strings
is drawn.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
version = 1

[layers]
base = "default"
fn = "fkeys"
media = "media"

[[layouts.default.zones]]
name = "main"
width = "fill"
modules = ["app\-controls"]

[[layouts.default.zones]]
name = "controls"
modules = ["status\-items", "mpris", "group/control\-strip"]

[layouts.firefox]
extends = "default"
[[layouts.firefox.zones]]
name = "main"
modules = ["key/Back", "key/Forward", "key/Refresh", "app\-controls"]

[[rules]]
name = "Terminals get F\-keys"
when = { app\-id = ["foot", "kitty"] }
layout = "fkeys"

[modules.clock]
format = "{:%H:%M}"
format\-alt = "{:%a %d %b}"

[modules.battery]
states = { warning = 30, critical = 15 }
format = "{icon} {capacity}%"
format\-icons = ["empty", "low", "half", "high", "full"]

[modules."group/control\-strip"]
modules = ["backlight/slider", "audio/slider", "audio#mute"]
drawer = { reveal = "tap", mode = "inline", collapse\-after = "5s" }

[modules."custom/vpn"]
exec = "~/bin/vpn\-status \-\-json"
return\-type = "json"
interval = "5s"
signal = 8
on\-tap = "~/bin/vpn\-toggle"
on\-hold = { open = "org.gnome.Settings.desktop" }

[gestures]
two\-finger\-swipe\-left = { layer = "media" }
edge\-swipe\-from\-left = { keys = ["LeftAlt", "Tab"] }
.EE
